WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.089
Good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.089 --> 00:00:06.380
So worldwide, more than 6 million children
died in 2013, which is horrible and unjust

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:07.470
and unacceptable.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:10.860
But it's also the lowest that number has been
in quite a while, even though the world population

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:11.860
has like steadily increased.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.800
Like, Hank, when do you think the last time
was that the world saw fewer than 6.3 million

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.570
children die in a year: 1975, when the population
of the world was 4 billion?

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:22.260
1900 when it was 1.6 billion?

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.119
No, in 1900 probably more than 8 million children
died.

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:31.110
Earth has not seen a year with so few child
deaths in hundreds of years--maybe a thousand

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:32.110
years!

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:34.641
So, Hank, I'm a big fan of the Gates Foundation,
the organization set up by Bill and Melinda

00:00:34.641 --> 00:00:38.399
Gates that is--favorite mission statement
ever-- devoted to the idea that all people

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:40.910
deserve the chance to live a healthy and productive
life.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:45.030
And Bill and Melinda just released this fascinating
letter highlighting three myths about development--and

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.890
yes, I can call them Bill and Melinda.

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:49.790
Perhaps you're not familiar with the rule
of twitter following (which I just made up)

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:52.739
whereby you can call anyone you follow on
twitter by their first name.

00:00:52.739 --> 00:00:55.660
See also my acquaintances Barack, Beyonce,
and Ellen.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.450
Right, but anyway, Bill and Melinda's three
myths:

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:00.950
First, it is not true that poor countries
will forever be poor.

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:04.920
Hank, I hear this all the time, especially
about Africa, that despite their rich natural

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.200
resources, "those countries" are just "doomed"
to stay poor.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.200
Well yeah, no.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:13.710
I mean, for one thing, seven of the ten fastest
growing economies of the last five years are

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:14.710
in Africa.

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:18.520
To quote Bill, "You should look skeptically
at anyone who treats an entire continent as

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:22.920
an undifferentiated mass of poverty and disease."

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:26.049
It is not fair that Bill Gates gets to be
both a billionaire and a good writer.

00:01:26.049 --> 00:01:29.430
Okay, it's time to put aside personal jealousy
and return to statistics.

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:37.200
Adjusted for inflation, Botswana's income
per person in 1960 was $383-it is now $12,000:

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.770
$48,000 for a family of four.

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:41.770
Now that's an extreme example, but this is
happening around the world--in the last fifty

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:45.960
years, income per person in India has quadrupled;
in Brazil, it has nearly quintupled.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.539
The second myth is that foreign aid is a waste.

00:01:48.539 --> 00:01:52.749
Okay, quick quiz--guess what percentage of
your countries budget is spent on foreign

00:01:52.749 --> 00:01:53.749
aid.

00:01:53.749 --> 00:01:56.369
The answer is three percent--if you're Norwegian.

00:01:56.369 --> 00:01:58.399
In the United States it's less than one percent.

00:01:58.399 --> 00:02:01.999
And even with that small investment, we've
seen tremendous results: twenty five years

00:02:01.999 --> 00:02:05.459
ago, there were 350,000 new cases of polio
a year.

00:02:05.459 --> 00:02:09.929
Today, thanks to the aid-funded polio eradication
initiative, there are fewer than 400.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:15.239
Malaria, and measles, and TB have all declined
dramatically, and healthier kids go to school

00:02:15.239 --> 00:02:18.579
more, and then they work more when they grow
up than they would if they were chronically

00:02:18.579 --> 00:02:19.620
ill or disabled.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:23.069
And the last myth is that saving lives leads
to overpopulation.

00:02:23.069 --> 00:02:26.269
I hear this all the time and it's just not
true!

00:02:26.269 --> 00:02:29.350
Population growth declines as infant mortality
declines.

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:30.470
All over the world.

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:31.650
It is that simple.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:36.719
To quote Melinda, "We make the future sustainable
when we invest in the poor, not when we insist

00:02:36.719 --> 00:02:38.269
upon their suffering."

00:02:38.269 --> 00:02:39.269
BOOM!

00:02:39.269 --> 00:02:40.799
The "boom" isn't part of the quote, that is-that
was my addition.

00:02:40.799 --> 00:02:44.380
In short, Hank, these investments are showing
phenomenal returns, and the greatest risk

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:48.390
we face is abandoning our success because
we wrongly think of it as failure.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:52.900
I'm gonna say it again: fewer children died
in 2013 than in any year on record.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:56.349
And all this means, just to be clear, a better
world not only for those living in poverty

00:02:56.349 --> 00:02:57.659
but also for the rest of us.

00:02:57.659 --> 00:03:00.799
I know this is counter to a lot of what you
hear on the news, but wealthier countries

00:03:00.799 --> 00:03:03.290
benefit when poor countries become less poor.

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:06.280
For one thing, there are more people on the
earth with the education and wellbeing to

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:09.629
make wonderful things, from paintings to smartphone
apps.

00:03:09.629 --> 00:03:13.000
But there are also more people to buy the
stuff that we make, whether that's artificial

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.010
lips or, for example, my novel The Fault in
Our Stars.

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:21.190
Hank, the Brazilian edition of TFIOS is called
A Culpa E Das Estrelas--(he said, butchering

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:22.190
the Portuguese).

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:25.079
Even though I can't say the title of the book,
it's sold hundreds of copies in Brazil--it's

00:03:25.079 --> 00:03:27.209
more popular there than in Germany or the
UK.

00:03:27.209 --> 00:03:32.030
A country once deemed incurably poor now has,
by some measures, a healthier book publishing

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:33.810
landscape than many countries in Europe.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:38.560
And it's not just Brazilians who benefit from
Brazil's phenomenal growth--it's also young

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:39.849
adult novelists in Indianapolis.

00:03:39.849 --> 00:03:43.810
So thanks to everyone in Brazil who's bought
my book and thanks to the Gates foundation

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:46.139
for decreasing world suck and busting those
myths.

00:03:46.139 --> 00:03:49.220
There's a link to Bill and Melinda's letter
in the dooblydoo; it really is worth reading.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:50.699
Hank, I will see you on Friday.

